# Per-install model override (optional).
#
# Copy this file to `agentic/models.local.yml` (gitignored — local to this
# checkout/machine) to override the model tier for specific agents. Any
# agent NOT listed here stays `inherit` (the canonical default for every
# agent in agentic/agents/*.md) — i.e. it uses whatever model your current
# session is running.
#
# Applied by `scripts/setup-agentic.sh <claude|cursor|all>` at install time:
# it rewrites the installed copy's `model:` frontmatter for each agent
# listed here, leaving the canonical source under agentic/ untouched.
# Re-run setup-agentic.sh after editing this file to apply changes.
#
# One line per override: <agent-name>: <model>
# <agent-name> is the agent's filename without `.md` (e.g. agentic/agents/do.md -> do).
# <model> is whatever your IDE/session accepts there (e.g. "haiku", "sonnet",
# "opus", or any model id/alias your Claude Code or Cursor setup recognizes).
#
# Example — if your environment has a cheap/fast tier available and you want
# the mechanical, low-reasoning agents to use it instead of inheriting the
# session model:
#
# do: haiku
# summary: haiku
# scrum: haiku
# codebase-explorer: haiku
# spec-validator: haiku
# plan-reviewer: haiku
# dev-reviewer: haiku
# sre-reviewer: haiku
# data-reviewer: haiku
# pre-plan-triage: haiku
# mcp-arc: haiku
# mcp-confluence: haiku
# mcp-gitlab: haiku
# mcp-jira: haiku
# mcp-glean: haiku
